   Prohibition created a black market that competed with the formal economy, 
   which came under pressure when the Great Depression struck in 1929. State 
   governments urgently needed the tax revenue alcohol sales had generated. 
   Franklin Roosevelt was elected in 1932 based in part on his promise to end 
